We apply the following patches to upstream source code.

libtomcrypt/math/ltm_desc.c:

1) Replace libtommath functions and macros deprecated since libtommath 1.2.0
   with their replacements.

   Each replacement is the definition of corresponding deprecated function
   in libtommath, which keeps behavior of libtommath math descriptor
   (ltm_desc) unchanged. Upstream made similar changes on its develop
   branch (commits c11287a0, 7c56243a, 3e11e86f, and a3310959), which are
   not yet in a release. Note that there get_int() uses mp_get_ul(), which
   changes its result for values that don't fit into 32 bits, so we don't
   backport these commits as is.

Patches were made as follows:

$ cd libtomcrypt/math/
$ mv ltm_desc.c ltm_desc.c.orig
$ cp -H ltm_desc.c.orig ltm_desc.c
$ edit ltm_desc.c
$ diff -u ltm_desc.c.orig ltm_desc.c >ltm_desc.c.patch

To re-apply them after upgrading upstream submodule:

$ cd libtomcrypt/math/
$ cp -H ltm_desc.c.orig ltm_desc.c
$ patch <ltm_desc.c.patch

Note that we symlink upstream source subdirectories as a whole, except for
math/, which we symlink file by file to be able to patch ltm_desc.c.
